                <pb facs="0597" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg513"/>

                <head>No. 258.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutelle to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >House of Representatives</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            10, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have just received a dispatch from Eastport, Me., stating that American boats
                    after herring for sardines at St. Andrews, New Brunswick, were driven away last
                    night by the Dominion cruiser Middleton, and it is announced that no American
                    boats will be allowed to take herring for any purpose. I earnestly invoke the
                    immediate attention of the Department to this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed>C. A. BOUTELLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
